{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792399355,"nonce":"Z5VkyH5eC4BICSrHUX7LyoGM+EQ=","title":"A ticker or timer that throws takes the other tickers of its tick with it, and the owners that keep a flag for theirs are left stuck","message":"**What happens**\n\nAnimationScheduler.tick takes the running tickers out of its list, calls each, and puts back those that returned true. If one throws, the exception leaves tick with the rest of the list gone: none of the other tickers of that tick is called again, and they are not in the list. A timer that throws does the same to the timers due with it. Anything that kept a flag meaning \"my ticker is running\" (the dashboard island's Sprung, the media Player, PointerQueries, Phone) then never starts another, so one spring or one clock stays still while everything else animates; if the exception reaches the loop, the whole program stops.\n\n**Fix**\n\nA ticker or timer that throws is dropped and reported (`ashui: a ticker threw and was dropped: ...` with its stack), and the others run as if it had not. Ticker gets `running`, false once the scheduler has dropped it for any reason; the island's Sprung and the Player ask it instead of keeping a flag. tests/fixtures/reactive/SchedulerFailures.hx has the checks.\n\n**Not found**\n\nWhat threw in the reports of single transitions stopping (the island's dropdown) is not known; the console message names it when it happens. PointerQueries and Phone still keep their own flags.","files":null}]}